<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <QuickAction> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
         matching parent xml file" error. It is also why there is no <description>: no quick
         action in this repo carries one (0 of 80 measured), QuickAction.Description is capped at
         255 characters, and a comment is repo-only and never sent to the Metadata API.

         ADDED 2026-08-26. User decision: "we don't need a quick action named 'Advance Stage';
         instead we need the NEXT STAGE NAME." One headless action PER DISPOSITION HOP, labelled
         with the stage the click lands on, replacing the single generic Advance Stage button on
         the DISPOSITION side of Contract_Review__c (the sell-side PSA).

         🔴 THE FIELD IS Negotiation_Status__c, NOT Stage__c. Stage__c on this object is DERIVED
         and unwritable - CONFIG_BY_TYPE records that explicitly - so both the page criterion and
         the server write name Negotiation_Status__c. A rule written against Stage__c here would
         look right and never fire.

         CONTRACT_REVIEW_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE maps 'Initial Draft' => 'Negotiation', so
         Contract_Review_Record_Page gates this on {!Record.Negotiation_Status__c} EQUAL
         'Initial Draft'. That literal is also DispositionStageEntryService's
         DISPOSITION_PSA_INITIAL_STATUS - the value every sell-side PSA is created at - so this is
         the first button an analyst sees on a new record.

         🔴 THE LABEL IS THE ONLY THING THAT DIFFERS BETWEEN THESE ACTIONS. Both point at the same
         c/advanceRecordStage bundle as Contract_Review__c.Advance_Stage; the target is derived
         server-side from the record's current status, per RECORD TYPE. Keep label and rule in step
         by hand.

         ACQUISITION IS UNTOUCHED. Contract_Review__c.Advance_Stage still serves Acquisition_PSA
         (Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed -> Executed) off its own separate map. The two maps were
         split on 2026-08-14 precisely so one side cannot aim a status at the other; do not
         collapse them, and note that 'Negotiation' is a value BOTH types carry, which is why the
         page rule pins the record type. -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Negotiation</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>advanceRecordStage</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
